data.content:
Here are the three breaking changes affecting your code in EF Core 10, with fixes:

---

## 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — now accepts a regular lambda (not an expression tree)

Your manual expression tree code **won't compile** because `ExecuteUpdateAsync` now takes `Func<...>` instead of `Expression<Func<...>>`.

**Fix** — replace the entire block with:

```csharp
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

---

## 2. Complex type column names are now uniquified / nested paths changed

Two sub-changes:
- **Same-name properties** across complex types (e.g. `Street`) get a numeric suffix to avoid silent column sharing.
- **Nested complex types** now use the full path (`Payment_BillingAddress_City` instead of `BillingAddress_City`).

**Fix** — pin existing column names explicitly:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, p =>
        p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, p =>
        p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
});

// For nested complex types, preserve old names:
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>()
    .ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment)
    .ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress)
    .Property(a => a.City)
    .HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City");
```

Or generate a new migration and apply the renames if you prefer the new defaults.

---

## 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

All methods (`CommandReaderExecuting`, `CommandReaderExecuted`, etc.) now require an additional `string logCommandText` parameter.

**Fix:**

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText)   // ← new parameter
    {
        // Use logCommandText for logging (constants may be redacted)
        // Use command.CommandText for the actual executed SQL
    }
}
```

Update all other method overrides (`CommandScalarExecuting`, `CommandReaderExecuted`, etc.) similarly.
